*Heading
Simply supported [0/90/0] square plate, S4R composite, sinusoidal pressure (quarter model)
** a = 1, plate 0 <= x, y <= a, this quarter 0 <= x, y <= a/2 with symmetry on x = y = a/2; q = sin(pi x) sin(pi y),
** one value per element (its centre). validate_with_ccx.py runs a/h = 100 and a/h = 10 and compares the centre
** deflection with classical laminate theory (Navier) and Pagano's 3-D elasticity solution.
** ccx 2.23 runs composite shells on S8R / S6 only: abq2ccx makes these S8R, with a node at the middle of every edge.
